That actually sounds fine to me. Nethack usually has ways to work
around its nastier aspects. This seems acceptable, especially since
it'll leave you a bit vulnerable (especially when dipping, quaffing,
or sitting for a wish). It also lends itself to hints through rumors
and/or or an oracularity, such as "They say that the wealthy should be
content."
Also note that the invocation artifacts and the Amulet of Yendor would
need special protection from this ("Your Amulet of Yendor shimmers
briefly, then stops."). Other artifacts might resist, or even be
immune.
This should not break polypileless conduct, but of course it would
break wishless conduct.
You might include a chance of the wish creating the item, possibly
aided by charisma, wisdom, and/or luck.
I also like the idea of creating special cases, like wishing for
dragon scales or dragon scale mail summons an appropriate dragon with
guaranteed scales. Similarly, you might include unicorn horns, golem
components, crysknives/worm teeth, and the like.

